      ]
    },
    "counter_defect_proof": "c1-count.py:51-52 PASS='pass' FAIL='fail' (lowercase); every refusal-leg string uses {PASS} (:160 expect_refuse, :223 FOREIGN, :234 SYMLINK_OUT, :315 ESCAPE_ENTRY literal) but :391 ref_pass = all(('=PASS' in l) for l in ref_legs) and :399 summary use uppercase '=PASS'. No refusal-leg string can contain '=PASS', so ref_pass is constant False and SUMMARY REFUSE constant 0/7. Executing the frozen aggregation block standalone against an all-pass leg set gives verdict=FAIL ok_pass=True ref_pass=False. Consequence: the frozen target 'c1-count.py must print C1=PASS and exit 0' is unreachable by any builder; C1=FAIL from this counter is not evidence of an unhardened builder, and REFUSE=0/7 is not evidence the refusal legs failed. Per-leg strings are the usable signal.",
    "counter_extras": {
      "item": [
        "c1-count.py:212 writes out-empty/spans/S777-1.txt, but that directory is created only by a successful EMPTY_OK; an always-refusing builder triggers FileNotFoundError: .../work/refuseall/out-empty/spans/S777-1.txt and the counter dies before printing any C1= line, so CONTROL_REFUSEALL=denied is denial-by-crash.",
        "SYMLINK_OUT is non-discriminating: expect_refuse receives forbidden_touch=[real/'spans.tsv'], a path that cannot pre-exist, and :233-237 overwrites legs[-1] with 'SYMLINK_OUT=pass(refused)' regardless; a builder writing through the link yields 'SYMLINK_OUT=pass(refused)(target-dir-written!)'. Neither string contains '=PASS'."
      ]
