    "frozen_state": "git diff 9e73a03 HEAD -- corpus/evidence/round58/c1-count.py is empty (frozen counter byte-unchanged). Lane HEAD=5da0a63. tools/build-spans.py is byte-identical to the pinned r55 control (diff empty) => base builder unhardened. S101 capture sha256 6063a3aff7a4081e93a685f2721e2cd6b477ba84a841211e298bcddd6d9fddf3, 129024 B, matches claims.md."
  },
  "risks": {
    "item": [
      "The frozen FAT_RAW fixture under-covers the hazard: it is OLE-magic + zeros, so capture-text rejects it as ole-malformed before any size path. It cannot detect the absent size bound; a valid oversized OLE is accepted by the base. Finding against the fixture's coverage, not fixed.",
      "The frozen predicate's C1=PASS is unreachable by any builder; either the case-sensitive comparison at :391/:399 or the lowercase leg formatting must change. L1's call; counter untouched.",
      "CONTROL_REFUSEALL=denied is vacuous as a control (denial-by-crash at :212).",
      "Scope limited to size/row bounds (seat item). FOREIGN, SYMLINK_OUT, SYMLINK_CACHE, FIFO_TXT, DEVZERO_TXT still fail on the base and are another seat's surface; my candidate does not claim them. The reference builder implements all of them but is a counter test vehicle only.",
      "The bound is a size/row bound only: does not bound text-size classes more generally, does not close the --out symlink race, does not address broader races (the claim does not claim those).",
      "_over_size + read(SIZE_CAP+1) bounds bytes, but a file replaced between stat and open is not identity-pinned; a same-size substitution between the two reads is not detected.",
