        "NEW_GROUND's base-side grep uses the wrong character form: it greps for traditional 載体类型标识 (U+8F09) but requires simplified 载体类型标识 (U+8F7D) in the entry. git log --all -S over corpus/knowledge shows neither form ever appeared there, so the grep returns rc=1 regardless; in a scratch probe I injected the simplified form into a base commit's citation-count-semantics-r37.md and the traditional-form grep still returned rc=1. Vacuously true this round (ground is genuinely new at base) - latent weakness, not a live bypass. The leg also needs a git worktree with the base commit reachable: against a plain directory copy (no .git) it fails with NEW_GROUND_FAIL.",
